Subject: GBA SIO: SD is high while a partner is on the cable; a parent writing start-bit 0 stops its transfer
Series-Step: 16/19 (mgba_dual 1.6-os4)
Origin: hanbang (this project)
요약: 링크 박자 1.4 — 상대 GBA 가 메뉴에 있어도 SD 선은 1(실제 케이블처럼), 부모가 전송 중 시작 비트 0 을 쓰면 그 전송을 멈춤. 사람이 순서를 안 맞춰도 젤다 · 유희왕이 붙음.

Multi-play SIOCNT bit 3 and RCNT SD read 1 whenever a partner is connected, even if it sits in a menu (GPIO input or
normal mode), like a real cable where nobody pulls the line down. A parent that writes start bit 0 while a transfer is
running stops it (no completion flag, no interrupt); children and solo play are unchanged. Two-GBA states carry
DUAL_STATE_LINK14 in the version field, so a 1.3 core refuses them and a half-updated pair cannot silently diverge.
Version string 1.4-os4.

---
diff --git a/src/gba/sio.c b/src/gba/sio.c
index 9f725d07add7..d89d375ede34 100644
--- a/src/gba/sio.c
+++ b/src/gba/sio.c
@@ -177,6 +177,17 @@ void GBASIOWriteSIOCNT(struct GBASIO* sio, uint16_t value) {
 
 	switch (sio->mode) {
 	case GBA_SIO_MULTI:
+		/* hanbang 1.4: the parent writing Start=0 while its transfer is still
+		 * running stops it (no completion, no IRQ). MultiSio's init writes
+		 * SIOCNT=0x2000 exactly for this; without it a transfer begun by the
+		 * previous protocol finished later and fired a stale IRQ into the
+		 * freshly initialized library (Four Swords title: host first = hang). */
+		if (!id && connected && GBASIOMultiplayerIsBusy(sio->siocnt) && !GBASIOMultiplayerIsBusy(value)
+		    && mTimingIsScheduled(&sio->p->timing, &sio->completeEvent)) {
+			mTimingDeschedule(&sio->p->timing, &sio->completeEvent);
+			sio->siocnt = GBASIOMultiplayerClearBusy(sio->siocnt);
+			sio->rcnt = GBASIORegisterRCNTFillSc(sio->rcnt);
+		}
 		value &= 0xFF83;
 		value = GBASIOMultiplayerSetSlave(value, id || !connected);
 		value = GBASIOMultiplayerSetId(value, id);
diff --git a/src/gba/sio/lockstep.c b/src/gba/sio/lockstep.c
index 993bbb9a1622..2952ccb80bde 100644
--- a/src/gba/sio/lockstep.c
+++ b/src/gba/sio/lockstep.c
@@ -897,11 +897,13 @@ static void _setData(struct GBASIOLockstepCoordinator* coordinator, uint32_t id,
 
 void _setReady(struct GBASIOLockstepCoordinator* coordinator, struct GBASIOLockstepPlayer* activePlayer, int playerId, enum GBASIOMode mode) {
 	activePlayer->otherModes[playerId] = mode;
+	/* hanbang 1.4: SD is a shared line that idles high; a cabled unit that is
+	 * not in multiplayer mode (title/menu: GPIO inputs or normal mode) does not
+	 * pull it low. Requiring every partner to already be in multiplayer mode
+	 * made the parent miss its one-time role check (Nintendo MultiSio: SD=1 &&
+	 * SI=0 -> parent) whenever it entered the link menu first. */
+	UNUSED(coordinator);
 	bool ready = true;
-	int i;
-	for (i = 0; ready && i < coordinator->nAttached; ++i) {
-		ready = activePlayer->otherModes[i] == activePlayer->mode;
-	}
 	if (activePlayer->mode == GBA_SIO_MULTI) {
 		struct GBASIO* sio = activePlayer->driver->d.p;
 		sio->siocnt = GBASIOMultiplayerSetReady(sio->siocnt, ready);
